From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:44:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virt_wifi: give the device its own lockdep classes

A virt_wifi device sends through its lower device, often a macvlan on an
Ethernet device. Its transmit queue locks have the class that every
Ethernet device gets by type, so a packet that goes down the stack takes
two locks of one class, one inside the other. With lockdep on, the first
IPv6 neighbour solicitation after boot reports possible recursive
locking in _xmit_ETHER and lockdep switches itself off for the rest of
the run.

Call netdev_lockdep_set_classes() when the device is initialised, as
macvlan, veth and vlan do. The device then has transmit, address list
and instance lock classes of its own, and its transmit lock sits before
its lower device's, which is the order the stack takes them in.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/virtual/virt_wifi.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/virt_wifi.c b/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/virt_wifi.c
index ff578d507527ef778a63d476593cdb1d16a1994f..03bab2641e579df48e4f80a07246b3b1e951aa1c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/virt_wifi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/virtual/virt_wifi.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <net/cfg80211.h>
+#include <net/netdev_lock.h>
 #include <net/rtnetlink.h>
 #include <linux/etherdevice.h>
 #include <linux/math64.h>
@@ -820,7 +821,19 @@ static void virt_wifi_change_rx_flags(struct net_device *dev, int change)
 				    dev->flags & IFF_PROMISC ? 1 : -1);
 }
 
+/* A virt_wifi device transmits through its lower device, so the two take
+ * their transmit locks one inside the other. Give this device classes of
+ * its own, as macvlan does, so that lockdep does not take that for the
+ * same lock twice.
+ */
+static int virt_wifi_net_device_init(struct net_device *dev)
+{
+	netdev_lockdep_set_classes(dev);
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static const struct net_device_ops virt_wifi_ops = {
+	.ndo_init	= virt_wifi_net_device_init,
 	.ndo_start_xmit = virt_wifi_start_xmit,
 	.ndo_open	= virt_wifi_net_device_open,
 	.ndo_stop	= virt_wifi_net_device_stop,
